OVERVIEW: Unified Procedure Step Worklist operations (UPS-RS)

Manages worklist items using UPS-RS protocol.

Examples:
  dicom-wado ups https://server/dicom-web --search
  dicom-wado ups https://server/dicom-web --get <workitem-uid>
  dicom-wado ups https://server/dicom-web --create worklist.json
  dicom-wado ups https://server/dicom-web --create-workitem --label "CT Scan"
--patient-name "Doe^Jane" --patient-id PAT001
  dicom-wado ups https://server/dicom-web --change-state <uid> --state "IN
PROGRESS" --aet MY_AE
  dicom-wado ups https://server/dicom-web --change-state <uid> --state
COMPLETED --aet MY_AE --transaction-uid <txuid>
  dicom-wado ups https://server/dicom-web --search --format dicom-json

--change-state performs Change Workitem State (PS3.18 11.7); --update is its
deprecated alias. A change to SCHEDULED is refused (PS3.18 11.7.1.4; PS3.4
Table CC.1.1-2, C303H). --format dicom-json prints the PS3.18 F.2 DICOM JSON
Model the server returned; --format json is a tool summary with camelCase keys.
  dicom-wado ups https://server/dicom-web --subscribe --workitem-uid <uid>
--aet MY_AE
  dicom-wado ups https://server/dicom-web --unsubscribe --workitem-uid <uid>
--aet MY_AE

USAGE: dicom-wado ups [<options>] <base-url>

ARGUMENTS:
  <base-url>              DICOMweb server base URL

OPTIONS:
  --search                Search for worklist items
  --get <get>             Get specific worklist item by UID
  --create <create>       Create worklist item from JSON file
  --create-workitem       Create a new worklist item from command-line options
  --change-state <change-state>
                          Change Workitem State (PS3.18 11.7) of the workitem
                          with this UID; use with --state
  --update <update>       Deprecated alias of --change-state (it performs
                          Change Workitem State, PS3.18 11.7, not Update
                          Workitem, 11.6)
  --subscribe             Subscribe to workitem events (requires --workitem-uid
                          and --aet)
  --unsubscribe           Unsubscribe from workitem events (requires
                          --workitem-uid and --aet)
  --aet <aet>             Local Application Entity Title for
                          subscribe/unsubscribe
  --state <state>         New Procedure Step State for --change-state: IN
                          PROGRESS, COMPLETED, CANCELED (PS3.18 11.7.1.4);
                          IN_PROGRESS is accepted for IN PROGRESS
  --transaction-uid <transaction-uid>
                          Transaction UID (0008,1195) for state changes
                          (required for COMPLETED/CANCELED; auto-generated for
                          IN PROGRESS, PS3.18 11.7.1.4)
  --filter-state <filter-state>
                          Filter by Procedure Step State (0074,1000):
                          SCHEDULED, IN PROGRESS, COMPLETED, CANCELED (PS3.3
                          Table C.30.1-1); IN_PROGRESS is accepted
  --scheduled-station <scheduled-station>
                          Filter by scheduled station AE
  --workitem-uid <workitem-uid>
                          Workitem UID (auto-generated if omitted)
  --label <label>         Procedure step label (e.g. 'CT Scan Chest')
  --patient-name <patient-name>
                          Patient name in DICOM format (e.g. 'Doe^Jane')
  --patient-id <patient-id>
                          Patient ID
  --priority <priority>   Scheduled Procedure Step Priority (0074,1200): HIGH,
                          MEDIUM, LOW (PS3.3 Table C.30.2-1; default: MEDIUM).
                          STAT is accepted and sent as HIGH
  --patient-birth-date <patient-birth-date>
                          Patient birth date (YYYYMMDD)
  --patient-sex <patient-sex>
                          Patient's Sex (0010,0040): M, F, O (PS3.3 Table C.7-1)
  --study-uid <study-uid> Study Instance UID to reference
  --accession-number <accession-number>
                          Accession number
  --referring-physician <referring-physician>
                          Referring physician name
  --procedure-id <procedure-id>
                          Requested procedure ID
  --step-id <step-id>     Scheduled procedure step ID
  --worklist-label <worklist-label>
                          Worklist label
  --comments <comments>   Comments on the procedure step
  --scheduled-start <scheduled-start>
                          Scheduled start date/time (ISO 8601, e.g.
                          '2026-03-20T14:00:00')
  --expected-completion <expected-completion>
                          Expected completion date/time (ISO 8601)
  --station-name <station-name>
                          Scheduled station name
  --performer-name <performer-name>
                          Performer name
  --performer-organization <performer-organization>
                          Performer organization
  --admission-id <admission-id>
                          Admission ID
  --token <token>         OAuth2 bearer token for authentication
  -f, --format <format>   Output format: table, json, csv, dicom-json (default:
                          table). dicom-json is the PS3.18 F.2 DICOM JSON
                          Model; json is a tool summary (camelCase keys)
                          (default: table)
  --verbose               Show verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

